    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0270" n="174" xml:id="pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.117/111: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-09T13:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 10—2:37
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>121. Legation telegram 71 May 12, 1:00 p.m., reported that Greek Government in
                    note March 31st designated Asia Minor campaign as new war. But Greek reply to
                    Allied Powers reported in Legation telegram 98 June 26, 1:00 p.m.,<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d163-f1"/> calls campaign continuation of old war. In view of this
                    contradiction I have requested Greek Government for immediate release from army
                    all classes naturalized citizens of the United States who have served in our
                    army.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
